    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d501">

                <pb facs="0508" n="1242" xml:id="pg1242"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Mr. Terrell.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-04-04"><hi rendition="#italic">April 4,
                        1895</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 409.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 460, of the 13th
                    ultimo, concerning the apprehensions of a massacre of Christians in Turkey, and
                    the presence of a United States ship of war in those waters.</p>
                <p>I have laid before the Secretary of the Navy a copy of your dispatch. I have
                    inquired of him whether the <hi rendition="#italic">Marblehead</hi>, now
                    understood to be at Gibraltar, could not be ordered to visit Smyrna, Adana,
                    Alexandretta, and Beirut, and by conference with our consuls and resident
                    citizens ascertain what foundation exists for the alarming apprehensions
                    expressed in that quarter, and if there be ground for anxiety to intimate to the
                    responsible authorities that the Government of the United States will afford
                    full protection to its citizens peaceably dwelling in that part of Turkey under
                    the guarantees of treaties.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
